1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,700
Everyone books the Yunnan package tour. Skip it. I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,100
Travel the old Tea-Horse Road your own way — Dali to Shangri-La.

3
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:07,600
Centuries ago, caravans hauled tea over these passes.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,000
No Tibet-style permit here — in Yunnan you go independently.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,500
The route climbs from 2,400 up to 3,300 meters.

6
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,100
You'll pass Tiger Leaping Gorge — 3,790 meters, peak to river.

7
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:17,600
Double-tap if you'd go your own way, not on a tour.

8
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,200
Stop where you want; the package bus never does.

9
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,800
★ Expert Tip: overnight in Lijiang to acclimatize before Shangri-La.

10
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:25,600
So: package tour, or your own route? Tell me I'm wrong.
